Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:45:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix the example analysis script so that it runs in lyse

The script added by pull request #117 tested `lyse.spinning_top`, which the
lyse module no longer has: `spinning_top` moved to `lyse.utils.worker` in lyse
commit 06ce8dc (v3.3.0rc1), so the script raised AttributeError on its first
statement after the imports whenever lyse ran it. It also saved a dict of the
two 254-element output arrays with `save_result`, which stores them JSON-encoded
in a group attribute and gives the lyse dataframe a column of nested series;
labelled the x axis "time (ms)" although the output table has one row per clock
tick; and kept an unused globals lookup, an unused pulse program, an unused
numpy import and comments copied from the camera example.

The script now takes the shot from `lyse.path`, which lyse sets to the shot
being analysed and which is None otherwise, saves the two output columns with
`save_result_array` and the maximum analog output with `save_result`, labels the
x axis "clock tick", and omits the unused code and stale comments.

Verified with the test harness on Python 3.14.6 with PySide6: the profile is
created with the script in it and the example experiment compiles; the script,
run the way lyse's analysis subprocess runs it, finishes against the compiled
shot and saves the `analog_out` and `digital_out` datasets and the
`analog_out_max` attribute in `results/example_analysis_script`, which
`lyse.Run` reads back and `get_dataframe_from_shot` includes as a column. The
script also runs in the deprecated standalone mode with the shot path as a
command-line argument. The harness lyse step passes on the same shot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
